<div class="container py-4">
  <h1 class="mb-4">About the BookStore Project</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    This application is a full-featured Book & Author Store built with Ruby on Rails, designed to manage catalog data efficiently using live external APIs.
  </p>

  <hr class="my-4">

  <h3>Data Source</h3>
  <p>
    All book and author records are fetched dynamically from the public 
    <a href="https://openlibrary.org/developers/api" target="_blank">Open Library API</a>, 
    requiring no authentication keys and ensuring a rich dataset of real-world literature.
  </p>

  <h3>Database Statistics</h3>
  <ul class="list-group mb-4" style="max-width: 400px;">
    <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
      Total Authors
      <span class="badge bg-primary rounded-pill"><%= Author.count %></span>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
      Total Books
      <span class="badge bg-primary rounded-pill"><%= Book.count %></span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD)</h3>
  <p>The database architecture follows a clean one-to-many relationship where an <code>Author</code> has many <code>Books</code>, and each <code>Book</code> belongs to an <code>Author</code>.</p>

  <!-- If you have an ERD image saved in your public folder, display it here -->
  <div class="card p-3 bg-light" style="max-width: 600px;">
    <p class="text-muted mb-2">[ ERD Preview: Author (1) <---> (Many) Book ]</p>
    <!-- <%= image_tag("erd.png", class: "img-fluid", alt: "Database ERD") %> -->
  </div>
</div>